1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,842
This is Aegis Treasury, an autonomous USDC treasury operator running

2
00:00:04,842 --> 00:00:06,398
on Circle's Arc testnet.

3
00:00:06,398 --> 00:00:09,788
Everything you are about to see is live, and every figure on

4
00:00:09,788 --> 00:00:11,692
this screen comes from the chain.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,204
Circle Gateway gives it one unified balance, and shows where that

6
00:00:16,204 --> 00:00:18,537
liquidity actually sits.

7
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:23,605
Idle cash goes to Earn Kit, next to the live USYC rate.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,254
Here is the interesting part.

9
00:00:25,254 --> 00:00:28,714
Limit orders, dollar cost averaging, and hedges.

10
00:00:28,714 --> 00:00:32,870
Conditions the treasury acts on with nobody watching.

11
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:37,703
I will arm a hedge. One EURC into USDC, the moment the oracle

12
00:00:37,703 --> 00:00:41,406
rate drops below two. Guardian evaluates it before it is even

13
00:00:41,406 --> 00:00:43,717
stored, and returns allow.

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,218
Now nothing happens on my side.

15
00:00:46,218 --> 00:00:49,307
A scheduler sweeps every sixty seconds.

16
00:00:49,307 --> 00:00:54,403
It reads the rate from Pyth, with staleness and confidence guards,

17
00:00:54,403 --> 00:00:57,689
so a frozen or a wide price simply does not trigger.

18
00:00:57,689 --> 00:01:01,857
When the condition holds, the policy engine gets the final word.

19
00:01:01,857 --> 00:01:06,954
Per transaction cap, daily limit, token allowlist, slippage bound.

20
00:01:06,954 --> 00:01:09,427
Only an allow reaches the chain.

21
00:01:09,427 --> 00:01:13,142
A denial parks the hedge instead of retrying it forever.

22
00:01:13,142 --> 00:01:16,161
This is the whole thesis of the product.

23
00:01:16,161 --> 00:01:20,410
The treasury is genuinely unattended, and it still cannot exceed

24
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:21,606
the rails I wrote.

25
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,658
There it is. Filled, with a real transaction hash on Arc.

26
00:01:27,658 --> 00:01:29,318
I never clicked execute.

27
00:01:29,318 --> 00:01:31,280
The scheduler did.

28
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,520
The audit log separates who did what.

29
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:40,733
I armed the hedge. Aegis executed it nineteen seconds later,

30
00:01:40,733 --> 00:01:44,750
for a dollar fifteen. Every allow and every denial is recorded

31
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,132
the same way.

32
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:51,263
This is the policy those actions were checked against.

33
00:01:51,263 --> 00:01:55,942
Because Arc uses USDC for gas, a limit written in dollars stays

34
00:01:55,942 --> 00:02:00,145
a limit in dollars. There is no gas token to model and no oracle

35
00:02:00,145 --> 00:02:01,921
sitting between the rule and the money.

36
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,296
Cross chain settlement runs on CCTP through Bridge Kit, burning

37
00:02:08,296 --> 00:02:12,801
on Arc and minting on Base Sepolia, with a reconciler that retries

38
00:02:12,801 --> 00:02:16,853
any transfer that burned but has not minted yet.

39
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,777
And the numbers are public.

40
00:02:19,777 --> 00:02:24,166
Fifty one bridges, real swap volume, paid inferences over x402,

41
00:02:24,166 --> 00:02:27,254
and a fee taken natively inside Bridge Kit and Swap Kit.

42
00:02:27,254 --> 00:02:30,853
Verify any of it yourself at guardagent dot org.

